{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120087","id":3825517516,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7kBMPM","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120087","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120087.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120087.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120087","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120087/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120087/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120087/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/8c2b92e5f7e8ad5ffbbe39de7a78e2094ba359bd","number":120087,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Windows: Fix `DirAccess::is_equivalent` for external and network drives","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> [!NOTE]  \r\n> I do not own a Windows computer to do testing on. I did test this with a Win10 Remote Desktop offered by my university. If someone can test on a \"regular\" Win11 device, I'd appreciate that.\r\n\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111702\r\n\r\nOn Windows, the `DirAccess::is_equivalent` method did return wrong results for certain more obscure drives like USB and network drives.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nFixes two things:\r\n\r\n- File handles need to be kept open while retrieving the file information. Relevant documentation:\r\n\r\n> The identifier (low and high parts) and the volume serial number uniquely identify a file on a single computer. To determine whether ___two open handles___ represent the same file, combine the identifier and the volume serial number for each file and compare them. [(GetFileInformationByHandle)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/ns-fileapi-by_handle_file_information)\r\n\r\n> The 128-bit file identifier for the file. The file identifier and the volume serial number uniquely identify a file on a single computer. To determine whether ___two open handles___ represent the same file, combine the identifier and the volume serial number for each file and compare them. [(GetFileInformationByHandleEx)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winbase/ns-winbase-file_id_info)\r\n\r\n- Adds a fallback in case the call to retrieve file info fails.\r\n\r\n`GetFileInformationByHandleEx` fails on the drives effected by this bug. Apparently it is not supported by all drivers, so a fallback is required. With this PR we also try `GetFileInformationByHandle` (which seems to have broad support). Just in case we fallback to a raw string comparison if that fails as well.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug",